description:
A shareable, named OpenSearch <a href='https://docs.opensearch.org/latest/analyzers/custom-analyzer/'>custom analyzer</a>. Decides how text is broken into searchable tokens — see the OpenSearch <a href='https://docs.opensearch.org/latest/analyzers/'>text analysis overview</a> for the high-level concept. The owned pipeline (char filters → tokenizer → token filters) lives in 'settings'; see TextAnalyzerSettings for the field shape. Example shape:

  {
    "organizationName": "biomed",
    "name": "scientific",
    "settings": {
      "tokenizer": { "name": "standard" },
      "tokenFilters": [
        { "name": "english_stop", "definition": "{\"type\":\"stop\",\"stopwords\":\"_english_\"}" }
      ],
      "indexFilterOrder":  ["lowercase", "english_stop"],
      "searchFilterOrder": ["lowercase", "english_stop"]
    }
  }

Reference this analyzer from a SearchConfiguration's defaultIndexAnalyzer / defaultSearchAnalyzer, or from a ColumnAnalyzerOverride, using its qualified name '{organizationName}-{name}'.
